Commands to send from your computer
Send this command	Robot action
forward	Move forward if the path is clear
backward	Move backward
left	Turn left
right	Turn right
stop	Stop the motors
sensors	Return distance and moisture readings
moistureon	Report readings every second
moistureoff	Stop periodic reporting
wateron	Run the pump for up to 5 seconds
wateroff	Stop the pump
Important before running it
1. Upload: disconnect HC-05 wires from D0 and D1 before uploading, then reconnect them.
2. Bluetooth: configure the serial terminal to 9600 baud and send each command with a newline.
3. First test: lift the wheels off the ground and test the motors before placing the robot on the floor.
4. Moisture calibration: DRY_VALUE = 800 and WET_VALUE = 350 are example values, not guaranteed readings for your probe. Measure dry and wet readings and adjust them.
5. Pump: use its separate 3–6V supply through the MOSFET circuit. The 5-second cutoff is a safety limit, not automatic soil-based watering.
Note: Because the HC-05 shares D0/D1 with USB serial, its data will also occupy the Uno's USB serial connection. Disconnect it whenever you upload a new sketch.
